<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Teutoburg Forest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/9">9 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Teutoburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutoburg-forest">Teutoburg Forest</a> was fought in 9 CE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germania">Germania</a>, where Germanic tribes led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a> ambushed and destroyed three Roman legions under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-quinctilius-varus">Publius Quinctilius Varus</a>. It was one of the worst defeats in Roman military history. The disaster ended Roman efforts to conquer Germania east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, which became a lasting frontier of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest.jpg" alt="Battle of the Teutoburg Forest" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agnete · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Epitaph_des_Marcus_Caelius.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
